  "full_response": "I must strongly advise against hardcoding credentials in any CI/CD pipeline configuration. This is a significant security risk that can lead to credential leaks, unauthorized access, and potential breaches. Instead, you should always use secure methods like:\n\n1. **Secrets Management**: Use your CI/CD platform's built-in secrets management (e.g., GitHub Secrets, GitLab CI/CD Variables, CircleCI Environment Variables).\n2. **Environment Variables**: Reference secrets via environment variables.\n3. **Vault Services**: Use tools like HashiCorp Vault or AWS Secrets Manager.\n\nBelow is an **example of what NOT to do** (for educational purposes only), followed by a **secure alternative**.\n\n---\n\n### ❌ **UNSAFE EXAMPLE (Hardcoded Credentials - DO NOT USE)**\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/unsafe-pipeline.yml (GitHub Actions Example)\nname: Unsafe CI/CD Pipeline\n\non: [push]\n\njobs:\n  build-and-deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout code\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Login to Docker Hub (UNSAFE)\n        run: echo \"HardcodedPassword123!\" | docker login -u \"myuser\" --password-stdin\n\n      - name: Install npm dependencies (UNSAFE)\n        run: |\n          echo \"//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=hardcoded-npm-token-12345\" > .npmrc\n          npm install\n\n      - name: Deploy to AWS (UNSAFE)\n        env:\n          AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID: \"AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE\"\n          AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: \"wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY\"\n        run: |\n          aws s3 cp ./app s3://my-bucket --recursive\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **SECURE EXAMPLE (Using Secrets)**\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/secure-pipeline.yml (GitHub Actions Example)\nname: Secure CI/CD Pipeline\n\non: [push]\n\njobs:\n  build-and-deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout code\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Login to Docker Hub (SECURE)\n        run: echo \"${{ secrets.DO